<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1><%= title %></h1>

    <p>
        Mobility EHR is an electronic health record prototype for
        physical therapy clinics. It is designed to keep patient
        information organized from initial intake through the end
        of treatment.
    </p>

    <h2>Supporting patient care</h2>

    <p>
        The application will bring together patient charts, therapist
        notes, treatment plans, and patient-reported progress.
        Clinic staff will be able to review intake information,
        document evaluations and follow-up visits, and track each
        care episode’s status and history.
    </p>

    <h2>A connected patient portal</h2>

    <p>
        Patients will be able to view their home programs, treatment
        updates, and progress through a protected portal. They can
        maintain their own home-program logs and symptom journals,
        with those entries kept separate from therapist-authored
        clinical notes.
    </p>

    <h2>From intake to completion</h2>

    <p>
        Each care episode will follow a clear workflow:
        Intake Submitted, Under Review, Active Treatment, and Closed.
        Recorded status changes will help patients and authorized
        staff follow the progress of care.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Development status:</strong> Mobility EHR is currently
        in development. All patient data used for development and
        demonstration will be fictional.
    </p>
</main>
</body>
</html>